he final round, but the gold medal was decided in a closely fought match in which Anderberg won over Evans by a split decision. Anderberg would win a silver medal at the 1954 Worlds, and compete at Melbourne in 1956, but he failed to medal at the latter tournament. Evans was NCAA Champion in 1952 and would repeat in 1954, also winning the AAU title that year. He also competed at the 1956 Olympics, both in freestyle and Greco-Roman, but without making the podium. Jahanbakht would win the 1954 World Championship in this class."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Medalists Match Record / Round Eliminated"] [:th {} "Bad Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "201"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59998"} "Olle Anderberg"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SWE.png"}] "SWE"]] [:td {} "2-0"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "346"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60621"} "Tommy Evans"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1-1"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "54"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58833"} "Tofigh Jahanbakht"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IRI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IRI.png"}] "IRI"]] [:td {} "0-2"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {